/*
The inputs to this function are:
- `src`: pointer to an array of signed 32-bit integers (input; read-only). It must contain at least `n` readable elements.
- `dst`: pointer to a writable array of signed 32-bit integers (output). It must have capacity to store up to `n` elements (since all elements could be positive).
- `n`: the number of elements to process from `src`.

Behavior (scalar loop):
for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    if (src[i] > 0) {
        dst[out] = src[i];
        out = out + 1;
    }
